# This corpus is BYTES, not text.
#
# core.autocrlf is true in this checkout, and one of the seven toolchains
# (Angular's CLI, on Windows) emits index.html with CRLF. Without this line git
# would normalise it to LF on commit and back on checkout, and the committed
# fixture would not be the artefact the numbers in README and BASELINE were
# measured on -- which is the entire premise of committing it. The probe reports
# "N bytes of HTML"; that N has to be reproducible.
#
# It also protects the built bundles from ever being rewritten by a future
# checkout on a machine with different settings. A minified bundle with its line
# endings changed is a different file with the same name.
* -text
